From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the GPU sandbox waits for /proc to drop joined
 threads

The kernel wakes a thread's joiner before it drops the thread from
/proc/self/task. A thread the GPU process joined just before
InitializeSandbox() could still be counted, and the GPU process then
ran without its seccomp filter: "InitializeSandbox() called with
multiple threads in process gpu-process". The tty VM test on a 2D
virtio card hit it in about 2 of 5 sessions.

- In the GPU process, InitializeSandbox() polls /proc every millisecond
  for up to a second before it counts threads as real.
- It logs how long it waited.
- A thread still there after a second (a driver's own) keeps upstream's
  behavior: a warning and no seccomp-BPF.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 sandbox/policy/linux/sandbox_linux.cc | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sandbox/policy/linux/sandbox_linux.cc b/sandbox/policy/linux/sandbox_linux.cc
index 12f64e9..7688240 100644
--- a/sandbox/policy/linux/sandbox_linux.cc
+++ b/sandbox/policy/linux/sandbox_linux.cc
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 #include "base/system/sys_info.h"
 #include "base/threading/platform_thread.h"
 #include "base/threading/thread_id_name_manager.h"
+#include "base/time/time.h"
 #include "build/build_config.h"
 #include "sandbox/constants.h"
 #include "sandbox/linux/seccomp-bpf-helpers/sigsys_handlers.h"
@@ -344,7 +345,22 @@ bool SandboxLinux::InitializeSandbox(sandbox::mojom::Sandbox sandbox_type,
     CheckForBrokenPromises(sandbox_type);
   };
 
-  const bool has_threads = !IsSingleThreaded();
+  bool has_threads = !IsSingleThreaded();
+
+  // Domicile's engine fork: the kernel wakes a thread's joiner before it
+  // drops the thread from /proc/self/task, so a thread the GPU process
+  // joined just before can still be counted here. Counted, it cost the GPU
+  // process its seccomp filter, at random. Wait up to a second for /proc to
+  // catch up; a thread still there after that is real.
+  if (has_threads && process_type == switches::kGpuProcess) {
+    const base::TimeTicks start = base::TimeTicks::Now();
+    while (has_threads && base::TimeTicks::Now() - start < base::Seconds(1)) {
+      base::PlatformThread::Sleep(base::Milliseconds(1));
+      has_threads = !IsSingleThreaded();
+    }
+    LOG(INFO) << "domicile: waited " << base::TimeTicks::Now() - start
+              << " for the GPU process's other threads to leave /proc";
+  }
 
   // The `options.allow_threads_during_sandbox_init` option is only used for
   // the on-device model execution process.
